{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["כי אין נִגְרָע — qametz in גרוע is the language of the present participle. If it had a pataḥ it would be past tense. So too נִשְׂגָּב has qametz, but נִשְׂגַב has pataḥ for past tense, and if it were past it should have been written כי לא נִגְרַע with pataḥ."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Rashbam's grammatical argument is somewhat ellipt: he distinguishes qamatz (present participle) from pataḥ (past tense) in pausal forms. The final sentence's logic is compressed and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:29.500345001Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}